    "body": "held on issue/3161-leads-sketch-height · commit a9db53e31 (local, not pushed - the machine disk is full) · worktree .claude/worktrees/issue-3161\n\nWhat I did:\n- Wrapped the `marks()` resolve in `crates/ui/src/start_exit_pick.rs` in `operation::display_heights(..)`, per the issue. A still frame now reads the sketch Z span frame memo.\n- Added a frame-cost pin, `start_exit_marks_read_the_sketch_height_through_the_display_memo`, in `crates/ui/src/egui_app/tests/contour_dxf_sketch.rs`: a DXF Contour with a From: Selection top height builds the sketch Z span once, then three further `marks()` calls build zero spans and take zero fresh reads.\n\nWhy I stopped (gate red twice, both environment failures):\n- The worktree machine ran out of disk. Gate run 1: `rustc-LLVM ERROR: IO failure on output stream: no space on device` during the ui build; every test step that ran was green, ui lib included (1431 passed).\n- Gate run 2: the disk-full run left mixed `thiserror` artifacts, then the retry build filled the disk again (`There is not enough space on the disk. (os error 112)`). The drive now reads 0 GB free.\n- No code failure in either run. The fix is committed on the branch; a worker with disk space can run `cargo xtask gate quick --base origin/main` and push.\n\nReleasing the claim. No effort change: the work stayed inside effort:low.\n",
